{"id": "EUVD-2026-103863", "enisaUuid": "ddddd903-1438-3230-a297-9d6a31bfbef2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbinder: fix is_failure flag for superseded transaction cleanup\n\nWhen a TF_UPDATE_TXN transaction supersedes a pending async transaction,\nbinder_release_entire_buffer() is called with is_failure=false. Since the\nsuperseded transaction was never delivered, binder_apply_fd_fixups() was\nnever called and no fds were installed in the target process.\n\nWith is_failure=false, the BINDER_TYPE_FDA cleanup handler interprets\nstale buffer contents as installed fd numbers and passes them to\nbinder_deferred_fd_close(), closing unrelated file descriptors.\n\nPass is_failure=true since the transaction was never delivered to the\ntarget, matching the semantics of all other undelivered-transaction\ncleanup paths.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:51", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e9b364e46d594c2ec663c9c49f10c1ca541ecc0f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/60a9f7323ae7318a7cce0d387c318da24f1e8726", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/86cdcc87d4ba60aebf94ba3346b3c900c5cd79ff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ab671b50714ad8e359cf37eb041d8044319ccdc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/22c135635fdd9816c0ef140d6de7b2e4fdf73e89"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98778", "GHSA-v997-cq9r-p9v8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "079cb242-3cdb-3b21-b1fb-600c226b6dd8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "397361b8-dfd5-313a-b785-470492f07e12", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "4fd2fd94-5e80-3551-a74c-a0feb9f6b387", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "568225e9-81d1-3007-8012-9f27356d4322", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": 